minimal b5e7 arg fix (its two bb1b calls passed the uninitialised param_5 instead of the real object).

ASM-verified (asm 0xbb1b-0xbb63, 0xc14f-0xc156; DS=DGROUP=0x1c00).  bb1b (a0ab twin): di=SELF near
offset in param_1; walks the 182-entry table @0xdfbc (stride 4), range-tests candidates via 0ea9 (host-
pointer coords) and, on a hit, dispatches c14f(si); Ghidra base-lost the walk (host-int stride 8) and
mis-nested the single loop.  c14f (a19e twin): si=object near offset; tail-jumps a type-specific handler
word[DG:(word[si]*2-0x1ae8)] with the object live -> passes it as a HOST POINTER (its handlers expect
one); Ghidra deref'd *param_1 host-ptr + dropped the arg.  b5e7 is dispatched by c0e5 with the object in
param_1 but reads it from the uninitialised param_5 (Ghidra host-ptr base-loss); its two bb1b calls now
pass (uint16)param_1 (the real object near offset).  0ea9/c14f carry via g_fist_cf.  (b5e7's own body
still reads the uninitialised param_5 -- a separate pending base-loss; this patch only makes the walk
crash-free.)  Mission-cascade only.
